---
title: Thai Green Curry
cooklang: 2
servings: 4
source: Joshua Weissman <https://www.joshuaweissman.com/post/easy-authentic-thai-green-curry>
course: dinner
cuisine: Thai
techniques: [toast, pound, fry]
---

= Paste ingredients [list]

@coriander seeds{2%tsp}
@cumin seeds{1%tsp}
@white peppercorns{1%tsp}
@green bird's eye chilies{9}
@serrano chilies{3}(seeded)
@shallots{2}(sliced)
@lemongrass{1%stalk}(tender core, sliced thin)
@galangal{2%cm}(peeled, sliced)|@ginger{2%cm}[if galangal is unavailable]
@makrut lime leaves{3}(ribs removed)
@garlic{7%cloves}
@coriander stems{4}
@lime{1}(zest only)
@shrimp paste{1/2%tsp}

= Paste -> paste

`Toast` the coriander seeds, cumin seeds and white peppercorns in a #dry pan{} ~{3%minutes}
until ~{fragrant}. Cool, then grind to a powder in a #mortar and pestle{}.

`Pound` the chilies with @-coarse salt{1%pinch} to a paste, then the galangal, lemongrass
and lime leaves, then the garlic, shallots and coriander stems, then the lime zest and
shrimp paste. Work each addition smooth before the next, about ~{20%minutes} in all.

= Curry

`Fry medium` @&paste{3%tbsp} in the thick top of @coconut milk{400%ml}(do not shake the can) in
a #wok{} over medium heat ~{5%minutes} until ~{the oil separates and it smells cooked}.

`Add` @chicken thighs{500%g}(sliced 1 cm thick) and coat in the paste ~{3%minutes}.

`Simmer` with the rest of the coconut milk, @fish sauce{2%tbsp}, @palm sugar{1%tbsp} and
@thai eggplants{6}(quartered)|@green beans{150%g}[if eggplants are unavailable] for
~simmer{10%minutes}.

`Finish off` off the heat with @thai basil{1%handful} and more @&fish sauce{} to taste.
